"s1-rl": {
"svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 440 150\" class=\"fig\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Reinforcement learning: the agent acts, the environment answers with a new state and a reward, and over many rounds the agent learns a policy that collects the most reward.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah-s1rl\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"ah\"/></marker><clipPath id=\"cp-s1rl\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"440\" height=\"150\"/></clipPath></defs><rect x=\"40\" y=\"50\" width=\"120\" height=\"50\" rx=\"6\" class=\"under\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"50\" width=\"120\" height=\"50\" rx=\"6\" class=\"box\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"71.5\" class=\"t\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Agent</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"86.5\" class=\"t\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(learner)</text><rect x=\"280\" y=\"50\" width=\"120\" height=\"50\" rx=\"6\" class=\"under\"/><rect x=\"280\" y=\"50\" width=\"120\" height=\"50\" rx=\"6\" class=\"box3\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"71.5\" class=\"t\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Environment</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"86.5\" class=\"t\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(game, maze)</text><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"62\" x2=\"280\" y2=\"62\" class=\"arr\" marker-end=\"url(#ah-s1rl)\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"54\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">action</text><line x1=\"280\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"90\" class=\"arr\" marker-end=\"url(#ah-s1rl)\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"108\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">new state + reward (+/−)</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"22\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">repeat many times → learn a policy: state → best action</text></svg>",
"caption": "Reinforcement learning: the agent acts, the environment answers with a new state and a reward, and over many rounds the agent learns a policy that collects the most reward."
},
"s2-ladder": {
"svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 440 230\" class=\"fig\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The attribute-type ladder: each type allows everything the one below it does, plus one more operation. Only ratio attributes have a true zero, so only they support “twice as much”.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah-s2l\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"ah\"/></marker><clipPath id=\"cp-s2l\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"440\" height=\"230\"/></clipPath></defs><rect x=\"12\" y=\"120\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" rx=\"6\" class=\"under\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"120\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" rx=\"6\" class=\"box\"/><text x=\"62\" y=\"138\" class=\"tb\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nominal</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"156\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">=  ≠</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"187\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">PIN code</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"201\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">blood group</text><rect x=\"118\" y=\"90\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" rx=\"6\" class=\"under\"/><rect x=\"118\" y=\"90\" width=\"100\" height=\"80\" rx=\"6\" class=\"box\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"108\" class=\"tb\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ordinal</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"126\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+  &lt;  &gt;</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"187\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">grades</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"201\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">rankings</text><rect x=\"224\" y=\"60\" width=\"100\" height=\"110\" rx=\"6\" class=\"under\"/><rect x=\"224\" y=\"60\" width=\"100\" height=\"110\" rx=\"6\" class=\"box3\"/><text x=\"274\" y=\"78\" class=\"tb\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Interval</text><text x=\"274\" y=\"96\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+  +  −</text><text x=\"274\" y=\"187\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">°C</text><text x=\"274\" y=\"201\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">calendar dates</text><rect x=\"330\" y=\"30\" width=\"100\" height=\"140\" rx=\"6\" class=\"under\"/><rect x=\"330\" y=\"30\" width=\"100\" height=\"140\" rx=\"6\" class=\"box3\"/><text x=\"380\" y=\"48\" class=\"tb\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ratio</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"66\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+  ×  ÷  (true zero)</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"180\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">kg</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"194\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Kelvin</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"208\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">counts</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"222\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"start\">← categorical</text><text x=\"428\" y=\"222\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"end\">numeric →</text><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"12\" class=\"arr\" marker-end=\"url(#ah-s2l)\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"16\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"start\">each step allows one more operation</text></svg>",
"caption": "The attribute-type ladder: each type allows everything the one below it does, plus one more operation. Only ratio attributes have a true zero, so only they support “twice as much”."
},
